From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:56:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] dt-bindings: mmc: mtk-sd: add mediatek,ckgen-delay

The driver sets the internal clock generator delay to one stage on every
host. A microSD slot on MT6797 reads data reliably at SDR104 only with
no stage. Describe a property for it, defaulting to the current value.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/mtk-sd.yaml | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/mtk-sd.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/mtk-sd.yaml
index 40f100f..c51d634 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/mtk-sd.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/mtk-sd.yaml
@@ -150,6 +150,16 @@ properties:
     minimum: 0
     maximum: 7
 
+  mediatek,ckgen-delay:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    description:
+      Delay stages of the internal clock generator (MSDC_PATCH_BIT0
+      CKGEN_MSDC_DLY_SEL). Some boards read data reliably only with this
+      set to 0. If not present, default value is 1.
+    minimum: 0
+    maximum: 31
+    default: 1
+
   mediatek,tuning-step:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
     description:
-- 
